 <text>
  <body>
   <p><note place="header">165</note></p>
<p><date when="1861">1861</date></p>
<p><date when="1861-01-24">24</date> 
<lb/>The <persName ref="cwgk:N00000258">Governor</persName> approved an account of $4. to <persName ref="cwgk:N00021429">H. B. Frayser</persName> for publication of the Governors Proclamation ordering election in place of <persName ref="cwgk:N00001579">P. Hines</persName> of <placeName ref="cwgk:P001020">Warren County</placeName>.</p>
<p>He pardoned <persName ref="cwgk:N00010882">W<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">m</hi></hi> Stewart</persName> convicted of burglary by the <orgName ref="cwgk:O001000">Jefferson Circuit Court</orgName> and sentenced to confinement in the <orgName ref="cwgk:O00000266">Penitentiary</orgName> for three years.</p>
<p>He respited for six months a Judgment of a <persName ref="cwgk:N00021607">Justice of the Peace</persName> for <placeName ref="cwgk:P00001509">Trimble</placeName> of $10. against <persName ref="cwgk:N00021424">Barney Williams</persName> for a breach of the peace</p>
<p>He respited for twelve months the following Judgments</p>
<p><table rend="rules">
<row>
	<cell><orgName ref="cwgk:O00000365">Carroll Cir. Ct.</orgName> vs. <persName ref="cwgk:N00021425">Jno. King</persName> -- </cell>
	<cell>$20. -- </cell>
	<cell>Gaming</cell>
</row>
<row>
	<cell>Do. Do. " P. Hundley</cell>
	<cell>$10 -- </cell>
	<cell>Selling Whiskey</cell>
</row>
</table></p>
<p>He remitted the following Judgments, to wit:</p>
<p><table rend="rules">
<row>
	<cell>Carroll Cir Ct. vs <persName ref="cwgk:N00021427">P. Hundley</persName></cell>
	<cell>$20. -- </cell>
	<cell>Gaming</cell>
</row>
<row>
	<cell><orgName ref="cwgk:O00000368">Cumberland</orgName> " " " <persName ref="cwgk:N00021426">Ballard</persName> &amp; <persName ref="cwgk:N00021428">Garman</persName></cell>
	<cell>$300.</cell>
	<cell>Misdemeanor.</cell>
</row>
</table></p>
<p>He approved and signed an Enrolled Bill Chapter 2.</p>
  </body>
